Q1.
Kafka stores messages for a configured retention period. To keep messages for 3 days, we need to set the retention time in milliseconds
1 day = 24 × 60 × 60 × 1000 = 86,400,000 ms
3 days = 259,200,000 ms
kafka-configs.sh --alter \
--entity-type topics \
--entity-name orders \
--add-config retention.ms=259200000 \
--bootstrap-server localhost:9092
This command updates the orders topic configuration so Kafka keeps messages for 3 days. After 3 days, older messages are automatically deleted, even if they have already been consumed.
